
Analysis Description
--------------------
Examine whether or not a codon alignment is better fit by models which
permit multiple instantaneous substitutions. v0.2 adds a separate rate
for codon-island triple-hit rates

- __Requirements__: in-frame codon alignment and a phylogenetic tree

- __Citation__: Submitted; preprint at hyphy.org/resources/fmm.pdf

- __Written by__: Sergei L Kosakovsky Pond, Sadie Wisotsky and Alexander Lucaci

- __Contact Information__: spond@temple.edu

- __Analysis Version__: 1.0


>code => Universal
>Loaded a multiple sequence alignment with **483** sequences, **466** codons, and **1** partitions from `/Users/alex/Documents/selection-tutorial/data/21-empirical/rbcL.nex`
The number of omega rate classes to include in the model (permissible range = [1,10], default value = 3, integer): 
>rates => 3

>triple-islands => No


### Obtaining branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases under the nucleotide GTR model

>kill-zero-lengths => Yes

### Deleted 20 zero-length internal branches: `Node146, Node207, Node229, Node279, Node347, Node362, Node42, Node496, Node573, Node582, Node633, Node685, Node722, Node725, Node730, Node771, Node796, Node811, Node815, Node924`
* Log(L) = -84171.84, AIC-c = 170288.48 (971 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site) 10.510

### Obtaining the global omega estimate based on relative GTR branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases
* Log(L) = -79470.86, AIC-c = 160865.92 (958 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site) 10.876
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio for *test* =   0.1890

### Fitting Standard MG94
* Log(L) = -75410.58, AIC-c = 152755.45 (963 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.1604
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.343               |    79.901     |                                   |
|               1.910               |    14.364     |                                   |
|               7.873               |     5.735     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -74742.28, AIC-c = 151420.86 (964 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.1330
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.2293
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.341               |    79.264     |                                   |
|               1.772               |    14.789     |                                   |
|               7.865               |     5.947     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -74664.76, AIC-c = 151267.84 (965 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.1326
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.1959
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.1827
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.1827
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.343               |    79.430     |                                   |
|               1.781               |    14.683     |                                   |
|               7.916               |     5.887     |                                   |


